From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Yoon <5332544+yoonda9@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 03:15:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] win: TAZ-only sync tests for the legacy fallbacks

Six tests for the event/semaphore sync primitives that the
legacy_fallbacks option swaps in. They sit in existing test files inside
the TAZ_LEGACY_FALLBACKS guard, so a stock build neither compiles nor
lists them.

  taz_once_race                    8 threads released together through a
                                   semaphore gate call uv_once; the
                                   callback runs once and no caller
                                   returns before it finished.
  taz_threadpool_wait_wake_stress  50 rounds of 64 uv_queue_work items on
                                   an 8-thread pool (set with putenv: the
                                   pool reads getenv, which on Windows
                                   does not see uv_os_setenv). Workers go
                                   idle in uv_cond_wait between rounds
                                   and each uv_cond_signal has to wake
                                   one; the whole run is bounded at 30 s.
  taz_sync_handles_balanced        GetProcessHandleCount is unchanged
                                   after 200 create/use/destroy cycles of
                                   a cond, a mutex and an rwlock, since
                                   the fallbacks own handles. The timed
                                   wait in each cycle has a zero timeout.
                                   Skips outside Windows.
  taz_rwlock_readers_share         a second reader gets in through the
                                   blocking uv_rwlock_rdlock while the
                                   first holds the lock; try-writers see
                                   UV_EBUSY while any reader is in, and
                                   try-readers see it under a writer.
  taz_cond_handoff                 100 rounds, each with a new peer
                                   thread, of two threads handing a
                                   counter back and forth 20 times, each
                                   signalling and then waiting on the
                                   same condition variable; in every
                                   other round the peer's first wait
                                   times out with the other thread
                                   queued. On Windows on one CPU.
  taz_barrier_rounds               five parties through 2000 barrier
                                   rounds, with exactly one serial party
                                   per round. On Windows on one CPU.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VxaFcyye2fdVEcaK7N8Jnn
